# Chapter 13 — AI & GraphRAG Engine Architecture

---

# 13.1 Purpose

The AI & GraphRAG Engine is the intelligence layer of the LexisGraph platform.

Its responsibility is to transform raw legal documents and organizational policies into structured legal knowledge and perform explainable compliance analysis using Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), Knowledge Graphs, Vector Search, and Large Language Models (LLMs).

Unlike conventional chat-based AI systems, the GraphRAG Engine shall reason over verified legal evidence retrieved from a curated Legal Knowledge Base instead of relying solely on the language model's internal knowledge.

The architecture shall prioritize:

- Accuracy
- Explainability
- Traceability
- Reliability
- Scalability
- Security
- Auditability

---

# 13.2 Objectives

The AI & GraphRAG Engine shall:

✓ Ingest official legal documents.

✓ Extract legal sections and clauses.

✓ Build a structured Knowledge Graph.

✓ Generate semantic embeddings.

✓ Retrieve relevant legal evidence.

✓ Compare organizational policies against regulations.

✓ Detect compliance gaps.

✓ Generate explainable recommendations.

✓ Provide confidence scores.

✓ Minimize hallucinations.

✓ Maintain complete traceability to original legal sources.

