# 13.4 Architectural Principles

The AI architecture shall follow the following principles.

## Evidence-First Reasoning

All AI-generated conclusions shall be based on retrieved legal evidence rather than unsupported model inference.

---

## Explainability

Every compliance finding shall include:

- Supporting legal clauses
- Knowledge graph relationships
- Confidence score
- Reasoning summary
- Source references

---

## Deterministic Processing

Document ingestion, parsing, graph construction, and embedding generation shall produce reproducible outputs for identical inputs.

---

## Separation of Responsibilities

The AI pipeline shall separate:

- Knowledge ingestion
- Knowledge storage
- Retrieval
- Reasoning
- Report generation

This modular architecture simplifies maintenance and future upgrades.

---

## Human Verifiability

Users shall always be able to trace findings back to the original legal documents and uploaded organizational policies.

